# Opening cutscene. One cue per part; the background for each part is set in
# Scripts/intro.gd (PARTS). Every cue must end with => END.
# The textbox fits about two lines: split longer sentences into separate lines.

~ intro_1
After a long drive home, you turn on the TV to watch your favorite show.
But instead, you are met with an emergency broadcast from the government.
=> END

~ intro_2
“ALL NORMAL BROADCASTING HAS BEEN DISCONTINUED DURING THIS EMERGENCY”
“AN INFECTIOUS FUNGUS THAT IS HIGHLY LETHAL HAS SPREAD RAPIDLY”
“INDIVIDUALS INFECTED DIE WITHIN THREE DAYS OF INFECTION
AND HAVE A HIGHLY CONTAGIOUS ROT ON THE RESULTING CORPSE.”
“THERE ARE NO VISIBLE SYMPTOMS OF THE CONTAGION”
“TESTING RESIDENTS FOR DISEASE IS RECOMMENDED.”
“SEEK AND REMAIN IN SHELTER AND WAIT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE”
=> END

~ intro_3
The broadcast suddenly turns to static.
=> END

~ intro_4
You live with your family on a small farm with an electric fence perimeter.
There’s a limited amount of food that you must manage carefully.
=> END

~ intro_5
You find old test strips in a box, although it is an energy-intensive process to use them.
=> END

~ intro_6
You must tend to your crops, as you can sustain yourself with what you can grow,
but making sure the perimeter is secure is your utmost priority.
Perhaps the old textbooks in your library might have beneficial information on how to deal with this crisis.
=> END
